{
 "note": "Skin recipes (0.13 Skins), taken over from the Blender interim version (blender/robot/skins.json, f8d1c5b) and mixed live by web/src/skinShader.js. Colours sRGB hex; layers apply in order. Reference: user picture of 29.10.2026 (three robots: rusty orange/navy, black with red glow lines, white/purple/gold). Roles: shell, accent, trim, graphite, dark_metal, anodized, rubber, energy, reticle_cyan. Layer selectors: roles, not_roles, parts, not_parts (glob on the part id; helmets through aliases), asm, side, facing [x, y, z, min cosine] (model axes, front +Z).",
 "edges": {
  "jumpDeg": 20,
  "roundDegPerMm": 18,
  "minTurnDeg": 8,
  "note": "plate edges for wear, bands and filigree (tools/skin_bake.mjs): open borders, shading-normal jumps > jumpDeg across an edge, and rounded strips where the normals turn faster than roundDegPerMm between two corners (≥ minTurnDeg, so tiny noise does not count; bevels of several segments turn little per segment). Blender version: 20° between texels of 1.1 mm."
 },
